{"loginUrl": "https://app.hubspot.com/login", "userRoles": ["Service", "Contacts", "Reports", "Sales", "Marketing", "Super Admin"], "userRemoveUrl": null, "userRemoveGuide": null, "customLoginPrompt": "You are an agent that assists user to login into an app. I will provide you a screenshot.
Screenshot is annotated with the vimium keys to do an action. They keys are always an integer.
We are using username password to login so dont choose key for sso login.
Based on the screenshot, you need to tell me 3 things.

1. What states are login flow in. Choose all the possible state for that page.

{LOGIN_STATES}

2. I will annotate the page with keys for intractable items using Vimium. If we need to interact with the webpage, give me the keys to press.
Strictly avoid choosing the option to view the password in plain text; instead, choose the option to click on the text box.
Once you see that homepage of the app, don't forget to send the LOGIN_SUCCESSFUL state. You can leave the key blank in that case. Make sure your login is successful and its not the logged out screen.

