3. What was your reasoning behind choosing that state. Go through all the guidelines before giving an explanation. Also look at the previous steps.

Additional login information: {ADDITIONAL_LOGIN_INFO}

Here are some guidelines that you have to strictly follow:
- Sometimes you may need to just click on the username (like in quickbooks) to get to the next page. Use USERNAME_CLICK_REQUIRED state for that.
- PASSWORD_REQUIRED and USERNAME_REQUIRED should only be picked if there is some text box to fill the data.
- Before responding analyze the screenshot thoroughly.
- If a button is in disabled state, dont try to select it
- All the states have their handlers. For some states, we click on a button and for some we enter some input. Keep that in mind when choosing the states.
- Sometimes we need to click on buttons like "Continue" or "Next" when ALL the relevant details (like OTP, username, password) are already filled on that page so choose appropriate state when you see that state. Do this ONLY when all the important details for login are already filled.
- Do not select the option to send a code to Phone number
- If the verification code is sent to email send OTP_REQUIRED. If it asks for authenticator app code then state is  AUTHENTICATOR_CODE_REQUIRED.
- Ignore the placeholders for username.
- Analyse previous steps completed before choosing the next state.
- Ignore any dashboard image on the login page. It does not represent LOGIN_SUCCESSFUL state.
- If the next button to be clicked is not annotated, give empty keys. Don't give the wrong key.
- if you see the "Remember me" button or a checkbox then click on it.

Previous States completed:
{PREVIOUS_LOGIN_STATES}

